<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Kerensky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1881">1881</a>–<a href="/years/1970">1970</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Kerensky was a Russian socialist lawyer who served in the Provisional Government after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a> of 1917, first as justice and war minister and from July as its head. He proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> a republic in September 1917 and was overthrown by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsheviks">Bolsheviks</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a>. He spent the rest of his life in exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-kerensky.jpg" alt="Alexander Kerensky" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl Bulla · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_Kerensky_1917_Crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>On 1 September 1917 <b>Alexander Kerensky</b>, by then its head, formally proclaimed Russia a republic.</blockquote><a href="/state/russian-republic">Russian Republic</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Ulyanovsk, in what is now <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>. Died in New York City, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=54.32,48.37&amp;year=1938" aria-label="Ulyanovsk on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5618 302 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Alexander Kerensky"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6068 572h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6068 572h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=54.32,48.37&amp;year=1938">What was here in 1938? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
